## Why this is an `.md.excluded` file (no scores)

- **SELF-EXCLUSION — zero verified public benchmark numbers.** Every benchmark row below reads `no verified public score found`: OpenCode Zen's own docs list the model with no scores, the community free-models comparison (auto-generated 2026-10-06) reports Intelligence Index / SWE-bench Verified / Terminal-Bench all `N/A`, and modelbenchmark.io carries a specs page with no measured values. Per the report rules, a model with zero verified benchmark numbers is saved as `<STEM>.md.excluded`, not scored. The queue's cross-rater average for this slug therefore does not include this file.

## Model card (specs only — verified)

- **Name:** Exo Free
- **Short description:** Free-tier preview reasoning model on OpenCode Zen — text and image input, tool use, 1M context — available for a limited time while the team collects feedback; during the free period, collected data may be used to improve the model (privacy note).
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen only (`exo-free`, endpoint `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions`, `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`). Publisher/lab not stated in any source found; "exo" also names an unrelated local-inference project (exo-explore/exo by exo labs), which is not this model.
- **Release / knowledge:** preview, release date and knowledge cutoff not stated.
- **IDs:** `exo-free` (OpenCode Zen; no Free ID — it *is* the free variant; no paid tier found).
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 tokens (community comparison table and modelbenchmark.io); max output 131,000 tokens (modelbenchmark.io).
- **Modalities:** text in; image in; text out; tool use yes; reasoning model (per modelbenchmark.io).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-10):** Free ($0.00 per 1M tokens, OpenCode Zen), limited time.
- **Architecture:** not stated in any source found — no verified public score found.

